WEBVTT

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:07.990
Hey, it's going to be okay!
We can fix this!

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.990
We just need to
get back to Headquarters.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.310
Which way to the train station?

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.830
I had a whole trip planned for us.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.470
(GASPS) Hey, who's ticklish, huh?

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.750
Here comes the tickle monster!

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:22.710
Hey, Bing Bong! Look at this!

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.470
(MAKING FUNNY SOUNDS)

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:26.990
Oh! Here's a fun game!

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.110
You point to the train station
and we all go there!

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.470
Won't that be fun? Come on,
let's go to the train station!

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.990
I'm sorry they took your rocket.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.870
They took something that you loved.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.390
It's gone. Forever.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.710
Sadness. Don't make him feel worse.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:46.790
Sorry.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.590
It's all I had left of Riley.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.790
I bet you and Riley
had great adventures.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.150
Oh, they were wonderful.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.950
Once we flew back in time.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.830
We had breakfast twice that day.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.150
Sadness...

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:01.630
It sounds amazing. I bet Riley liked it.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.710
(SNIFFLING) Oh, she did.
We were best friends.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:08.630
Yeah. It's sad.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.510
(CRYING)

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.430
Wh...

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.030
(GROANS)

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.390
I'm okay now.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.030
Come on. The train station is this way.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.790
How did you do that?

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.030
Oh, I don't know. He was sad.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:38.350
So I listened to what...

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.230
Hey! There's the train!

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:41.870
(TRAIN HONKING HORN)

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.550
(ALL GRUNTING)

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.950
Oh! We made it!
We're finally going to get home!

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.550
Oh, no! These Facts and Opinions
look so similar.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.830
Oh, don't worry about it.
Happens all the time.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.270
(GRUNTS)

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:07.710
On a scale of one to ten,

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.270
I give this day an F.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:12.150
Well, why don't we quit standing
around and do something?

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.270
Like what, genius?

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.270
Like quitting. That's what I'm doing.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.270
Sure it's the coward's way out.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.390
But this coward's gonna survive.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.590
Ow!

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:25.790
(EXCLAIMING)

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.910
DISGUST: Emotions can't quit, genius!

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.790
Ugh! I thought we were supposed to
be keeping Riley happy.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.950
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.270
Mmm.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.390
Aha! (LAUGHING)

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.150
-What is it?
-Oh, nothing.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.510
-Just the best idea ever.
-What?

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.230
All the good Core Memories

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.470
were made in Minnesota.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.630
Ergo, we go back to Minnesota
and make more.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:51.790
-Ta-da!
-FEAR: Wait, wait, wait.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.750
You're saying we run away?

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:55.310
Well, I wouldn't call it that.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:57.870
I'd call it the Happy Core
Memory Development program.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.270
You can't be serious.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:00.630
Hey! Our life was perfect

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.150
until Mom and Dad decided to move to

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.790
San Fran Stinktown.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.070
(STAMMERING) I mean,
it's just so drastic!

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.310
Need I remind you
of how great things were there?

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.150
Our room? Our back yard?

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.270
Our friends?

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.630
MAN: ♪ TripleDent gum
WOMAN: ♪ Will make you smile ♪

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.630
-Did I ask for the gum commercial?
-(SONG STOPS PLAYING)

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.510
Anyway, it was better, that's my point.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:22.150
Yeah, Riley was happier in Minnesota.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.390
Wait. Hold on. Shouldn't we
just sleep on this or something?

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.190
Fine. (CHUCKLES) Let's sleep on it.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.190
Because, hey,
I'm sure jolly fun-filled times

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.230
are just around the corner.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.710
Huh?

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.190
Hey, hey! Why aren't we moving?

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.590
Riley's gone to sleep.
We're all on break.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.550
You mean we're stuck
here until morning?

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.510
Yeah, the Train of Thought
doesn't run while she's asleep.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.870
Oh, we can't wait that long.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.070
-How about we wake her up?
-Sadness, that's ridiculous!

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.830
How could we possibly... (GASPS)

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:00.710
JOY: How about we wake her up?

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.830
-Great idea, Joy.
-Thanks. Come on!

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.270
Whoa! This place is huge!

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.990
Yeah, it looks so much smaller
than I expected.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.030
Wow! I Can Fly?

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.830
BING BONG: I love that one!

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:20.310
(GASPS) Rainbow Unicorn!
She's right there!

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.350
My friend says you're famous.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.470
She wants your autograph.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:29.150
No, no, Sadness,
don't bother Miss Unicorn, okay?

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.550
Sorry, she's from out of town.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:31.910
That was so embarrassing, right?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.710
I loved you in
Fairy Dream Adventure Part 7.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:36.790
Okay, bye. I love you!

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.390
Huh. Wonder what that means.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:41.750
Oh, well, let's go in.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:45.670
DIRECTOR: Set up the classroom set!

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:46.910
DIRECTOR: Today's memories are in!

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.710
DIRECTOR: We've got
a lot to work with here.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.150
Riley dumped her best friend,

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.710
had a miserable day at school,

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:52.790
and quit hockey.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.990
DIRECTOR: The writers have
put together a killer script!

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.190
Just because Joy
and Sadness are gone,

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.750
I have to do stupid Dream Duty.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:00.390
(GRUMBLING)

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.550
Okay. How are we going to wake her up?

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.510
Well, she wakes up sometimes
when she has a scary dream.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.230
-We could scare her.
-Scare her?

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.030
No, she's been through enough already.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:10.590
-But, Joy...
-Sadness, you may know your way

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.510
around down here, but I know Riley.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:13.870
We're gonna make her so happy,

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.070
she'll wake up with exhilaration.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:17.510
We'll excite her awake!

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.430
That's never happened before.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.430
(GASPS) Ooh!
Riley loves dogs. Put this on.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:22.590
I don't think that'll work.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.750
-Bing Bong?
-BING BONG: Yeah?

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.550
Don't let anything happen to these.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:27.790
Got it.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:30.710
Mmm-hmm. Add the reality
distortion filter.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.590
Love it. Remember,
play to the camera, everyone!

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.030
Riley is the camera!

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.310
DIRECTOR: Makeup,
get out of there, we are on in five,

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:40.670
four, three...

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.030
(STRUMMING DREAMY MUSIC)

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.470
Hello, class.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.470
Before we begin today's pop quiz...

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.270
Man, she is one bad actress.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.110
...which counts for 90%
of your final grade,

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.950
I want to introduce
our new student. Riley.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.070
Would you like to stand up

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.550
-and introduce yourself?
-Camera.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:04.110
-And cue Riley.
-(CLEARS THROAT)

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:05.870
(IN RILEY'S VOICE)
My name is Riley Andersen.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.830
I'm from Minnesota and now I live here.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.350
Ew, look! Her teeth are falling out!

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.350
-That's disgusting.
-Ew, gross!

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.630
Teeth falling out. (SPITS)

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:16.990
Yeah, I'm used to that one.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.150
(SLURPS)

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.950
Let me guess, we have no pants on.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.310
Hey, look!
She came to school with no pants on!

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.430
-FEAR: Called it!
-Ready?

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.590
I don't think
this happy thing is going to work.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:27.710
But if we scare her...

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.350
Just follow my lead. Here we go.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:30.910
(SCREAMING)

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.710
Bark! Bark! Bark!

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.590
-Who is that?
-Uh, what's going on?

